  "homeActivities": [
    {
      "text": "Activity 1 — The bean in a glass (8 days)\nPush wet cotton wool into a clear glass. Slide two or three dry beans down the side of the glass so they are pressed against it and he can\nwatch them. Keep the cotton damp. Every morning he looks and draws what he sees.\nDay 1: nothing. Day 4: a small white root pushes downwards. Day 7: a shoot pushes upwards. Day 8: the first tiny green leaves open.\nActivity 2 — The light test (9 days)\nPlant two young beans the same way in two pots. Put one on a sunny windowsill and one inside a dark cupboard. Water both exactly the\nsame. After nine days, bring them together and compare. The plant in the light is green, short and strong. The plant in the dark is pale\nyellow, long, thin and floppy. He will never forget that plants need light.",
      "safety": "An adult stays with the child for every activity. No glass, no sockets, no flames, and nothing small enough to swallow is left with a child\nalone. Water activities are done in a bowl or the sink, never near electrical items.",
      "pages": [
        6,
        7
      ],
